#! ia 1.0

@convention catalogue-description-length
  meaning
    says "A skill description states what the skill does and when to use it, in at most 400 characters. tools/validate.py requires <= 400 and TRIGGER.search (message: skill description needs what and when) against TRIGGER = re.compile, a pattern that accepts use this, it, when, for, to, after, before, at, in, on, once or as, or the word when."
    answers "How long may a skill description be, and what must it say?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Keep every skill description at most 400 characters and include a use-when trigger phrase."
  subject
    subject-word capability

@convention catalogue-model-invocable-limit
  meaning
    says "A plugin has at most four model-invocable skills. tools/validate.py sets MODEL_INVOCABLE_PER_PLUGIN = 4 and refuses a plugin with more (message: too many model-invocable skills in), naming them; a skill is model-invocable unless its frontmatter carries disable-model-invocation: true, so the stage skills reached by path set it."
    answers "How many skills of one plugin may a model invoke on its own?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Give a plugin at most four model-invocable skills; mark every other skill disable-model-invocation: true."
  subject
    subject-word capability

@convention catalogue-listing-budget
  meaning
    says "The catalogue's skill listing stays within 7,500 characters. tools/validate.py sets LISTING_BUDGET = 7500 as the names plus descriptions of every skill in the catalogue and refuses a catalogue over it (message: skill listing over budget), because Codex ignores disable-model-invocation and lists every skill."
    answers "How much listing text may all the skills of the catalogue spend together?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Keep the folder names plus descriptions of all skills in the catalogue within 7,500 characters."
  subject
    subject-word capability

@convention catalogue-hidden-description
  meaning
    says "A hidden skill, one with disable-model-invocation: true, has a description of at most 160 characters. tools/validate.py sets HIDDEN_DESCRIPTION = 160 because stage skills are reached by path while Codex still lists them, and refuses a longer one (message: hidden skill description over); the entry skill of a plugin named in UNADVERTISED keeps the 400-character budget instead."
    answers "How long may the description of a hidden skill be?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Keep the description of every hidden skill at most 160 characters."
  subject
    subject-word capability

@convention catalogue-codex-bridge
  meaning
    says "Every skill opens its body with the Codex bridge line. tools/validate.py defines CODEX_BRIDGE = re.compile as a line that starts with the bold Codex label and links ../../CODEX.md, and refuses a skill whose first body line does not match it (message: skill must open with the Codex bridge line), because Codex lists every skill and may load a stage skill directly."
    answers "What must the first body line of every skill be?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Open every skill body with the Codex bridge line that links ../../CODEX.md."
  subject
    subject-word capability

@convention catalogue-qualified-hooks
  meaning
    says "Only the plugins listed in QUALIFIED_HOOKS ship hooks, and each ships exactly the qualified set. tools/validate.py names each hook plugin with each event, matcher, script, argument and timeout, and refuses a hooks.json that differs from it (message: hooks differ from the qualified set), so a widened matcher, a rewired or dropped handler, an added event or a changed timeout fails. The runtime files named in RUNTIME_FILES, hooks.json among them, are refused in every other plugin (message: runtime component not admitted), and runtime_keys refuses runtime components in skill and agent frontmatter."
    answers "Which plugins may carry hooks, and what must those hooks equal?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Add no hook to a plugin that QUALIFIED_HOOKS does not list, and never change a qualified hook without a decision that updates the set."
  subject
    subject-word capability

@convention catalogue-agent-allowlist
  meaning
    says "An agent declares a tools allowlist. tools/validate.py refuses an agent whose tools value is empty, * or [], or that sets disallowedTools (message: agent needs a tools allowlist), because a denylist still inherits Agent, PowerShell, Skill and every MCP tool."
    answers "How must a plugin agent declare the tools it may use?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Give every agent an explicit tools allowlist; never a wildcard, an empty list or a denylist."
  subject
    subject-word capability

@convention catalogue-author-licence
  meaning
    says "A plugin manifest names its author as an object with a name, and its license is the catalogue's own licence: Apache-2.0 in a public catalogue. schemas/plugin-manifest.schema.json requires the author property with a required, non-empty name and no other property, and fixes license to the catalogue's licence, so a manifest that names another licence is refused."
    answers "What author and licence does a plugin manifest carry?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Write the author as an object with only a name and the license as the catalogue's licence (Apache-2.0 in a public catalogue) in every plugin manifest."
  subject
    subject-word capability

@convention catalogue-author-is-not-reviewer
  meaning
    says "The author of a plugin change is never its reviewer. A reviewer who wrote any part of the change reviews nothing of it, a finding is confirmed by someone other than the reviewer who raised it before it blocks, and a blocking finding blocks the merge until it is fixed or the catalogue's owner records why it may wait. The catalogue records its review process as a decision in docs/decisions.md."
    answers "Who may review a plugin change?"
  governance
    severity blocking
    requires "Have every plugin change reviewed by someone other than the person or agent that wrote it."
  subject
    subject-word capability
